    "title": "Euclid pool slated for $1 million-plus in renovations, repairs - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Frank Mecham fmecham@news-herald.com ,\n21 hours ago Euclid’s Ralph V. Hill Memorial Pool, commonly known by residents as just Memorial Pool, will be getting a facelift for essentially the first time since it opened in 1954. City Council members recently voted to spend up to $1,175,000 for upgrades and renovations and repairs to the pool house, structure, and common areas of the aging facility located at 22450 Milton Ave., which has been a common meeting area for residents during its history. Read full article\n2",
